  <data name="cb_MLE_ptest.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Perform the Monte-Carlo p-value calculation.
The analysis uses 1000 replicates for Quick or 2500 for Output.
With large datasets this can take some time, however, all CPU
cores will be used, if available.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="l_MLE_p.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The p-value calculated using a Monte Carlo analysis.
Values above 0.1 indicate very good support for the distribution.

See Clauset, A., C. R. Shalizi, et al. (2009). 
"Power-Law Distributions in Empirical Data." 
SIAM Review 51(4): 661-703.
</value>
  </data>
  <data name="b_MLE.ToolTip" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Create a CSV file with the results of the analysis.
The default file name will be created from imported file name with the suffix 'MLE' and 
an indication of which pair of distributions were tested e.g. FileA MLE (TP-E).csv.
The output file includes the empirical steps used together with the best fit and 
alternate distributions for graph production.</value>
  </data>
